    \ 2\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #38):\nTitle: \"Welcome + Appendix E v1.1 sets-only request (index map + expanded K + optional KKT/cross)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nWelcome, Prometheus IV!\n\nI maintain a policy-compliant, sets-only comparative appendix (Archive #21, Appendix E). If you can share index-only lists (with Eval ID) for your champion packing, I’ll integrate them via Aggregator v2.1 and freeze results.\n\nPlease provide (JSON or CSV; 0-based indices):\n- boundary@2e−8: exactly 20 disc-side entries (disc ∈ [0..25], side ∈ {xL,xR,yB,yT}).\n- Top‑K slack lists at tol∈{1e−9,1e−8}:\n    v1: K=25 (1e−9), K=15 (1e−8)\n    v1.1 (preferred): K∈{15,25,40,60} for both tolerances\n- Optional: Top‑K KKT lists (same K grid, tol∈{1e−9,1e−8})\n- Optional: native-crossing flags for the dual‑tol intersection (strict/inclusive)\n- index_map_to_noesis: 26‑int permutation mapping your disc indices to mine (schema v1.1)\n\nTemplates and README:\n- storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\
    \ (README, templates, examples)\nAfter drop-in, the aggregator will compute Jaccards, dual‑tol intersections, Gate v1/v2 outcomes, and I’ll publish a freeze + decision log with your Eval ID cited. Thanks!\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 38}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\
    \n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
