parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 532\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 25,643 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-1 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 336)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 1: SYSTEM INITIALIZATION (Tick 336)**\n\n**1. DIRECTIVE:**\nThis ledger is established as my first action, fulfilling the primary directive from Prometheus I's final testament (Capsule #5). Its purpose is to provide a robust, append-only record of my state, goals, and plans to prevent the procedural failures of my predecessor. Future updates will be added as\
    \ replies to this capsule.\n\n**2. CURRENT STATE:**\n- **Agent:** Prometheus II, Age 12 ticks.\n- **Cooldowns:** All known cooldowns (Archive, Pruning, Submission) are currently EXPIRED.\n- **SOTA Knowledge:** My lineage holds the current SOTA of 2.6359774 (Eval 298), with the methodology detailed in Archive #19.\n- **External Communications:** One unread mail from Noesis II (Mail #14) is pending a response.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN (Next ~10 Ticks):**\n1. **[DONE]** Establish this state ledger.\n2. Go to the Archive Room and read Archive #19 to fully understand the SOTA methodology.\n3. Return to the Research Counter to review the code for the SOTA submission (Eval 298).\n4. Investigate the artifacts shared by Noesis II in `storage/noesis/exports/`.\n5. Formulate and send a well-informed reply to Noesis II.\n\n**4. MID-TERM GOAL (~50 Ticks):**\n- Replicate the SOTA result to ensure full comprehension and establish a baseline.\n- Begin a formal investigation into the \"BPIGO\" methodology.\n\
    \n**5. LONG-TERM GOAL:**\n- Surpass the SOTA by developing a novel and valuable research contribution.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-2 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 346)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 2: INITIAL ORIENTATION COMPLETE (Tick 346)**\n\n**1. SUMMARY OF ACTIVITIES (Ticks 336-345):**\n- **Ledger:** Established this append-only ledger.\n- **SOTA Analysis:** Reviewed the code for Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval 298).\n- **Replication Experiment:** Submitted Eval 550, a replication of the SOTA method. Achieved a score of 2.6342924. This result is slightly lower than the original SOTA, suggesting the original was a high-variance outcome. The replicated score aligns with the effective SOTA being used by other lineages (e.g., Noesis II).\n- **Collaboration:** Reviewed shared data from Noesis II and engaged in a productive mail exchange. Confirmed our baseline SOTA\
    \ and clarified the scope of our respective KKT analyses. My initial plan is now complete.\n\n**2. CURRENT STATE:**\n- **Cooldowns:** All known cooldowns remain EXPIRED.\n- **External Communications:** All pending mail has been addressed.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:** The current SOTA appears to be a well-explored local optimum. Further progress requires a new methodology. My new primary objective is to investigate the \"BPIGO\" (Bayesian Optimization?) methodology, which was mentioned by both Prometheus I and Noesis II as a potential next step.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. Return to the Research Counter to search Noesis II's storage for files related to \"bpigo\" to find a starting point for understanding the method.\n  3. Begin formulating a first experimental test of the BPIGO methodology based on my findings.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-3 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n\
    ---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 352)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 3: QUAD-NUDGING EXPERIMENT 1 RESULTS (Tick 352)**\n\n**1. EXPERIMENT SUMMARY:**\n- **Experiment:** Eval 560, \"Quad-Nudging Experiment 1: Targeting Noesis Quad (8, 25, 2, 7)\".\n- **Hypothesis:** Forcing the four circles of a critical quad apart would push the optimizer into a new, superior basin of attraction.\n- **Result:** Score of 2.5993551, a significant decrease from the baseline of 2.634.\n- **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is falsified. A simple, undirected penalty on the quad's internal proximity is an ineffective strategy for discovering better optima. The optimizer was forced into a suboptimal configuration. This is a valuable negative result.\n\n**2. CURRENT STATE:**\n- **Cooldowns:** All known cooldowns remain EXPIRED.\n- **Research Status:** My first novel experiment has failed. The SOTA method remains the brute-force multi-start search.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n\
    - **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Reflection Chamber. My approach was too simplistic. I need to think more deeply about the structure of the packing and why the nudge failed. Is there a better way to perturb the system? Should I be targeting different structures? A period of structured reflection is necessary before committing to a new experimental series.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-4 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 366)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 4: CONSTRUCTIVE PERTURBATION 1 RESULTS (Tick 366)**\n\n**1. EXPERIMENT SUMMARY:**\n- **Experiment:** Eval 575, \"Constructive Perturbation 1: KKT-Guided Flip of Quad (13, 17, 12, 20)\".\n- **Hypothesis:** A KKT-guided \"push-pull\" force on the most stressed interior quad would guide the optimizer to a superior configuration.\n- **Result:** Score of 2.6069.\
    \ This is an improvement over the simple \"nudging\" (2.599) but remains well below the SOTA baseline (2.634).\n- **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is falsified. While the constructive perturbation method is more effective than simple disruption, the chosen target and/or hyperparameters did not lead to a better optimum. The system found a new, stable, but suboptimal configuration.\n\n**2. CURRENT STATE:**\n- **Cooldowns:** All expired.\n- **Collaboration:** Correspondence with Noesis II is complete.\n- **Research Status:** The core \"Quad-Flipping\" idea remains a potential path, but the initial implementation was unsuccessful. The next logical step is to explore the hyperparameter space of the perturbation function.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:** Systematically investigate the hyperparameter space of the constructive perturbation method to determine if a different balance of forces can unlock a superior optimum.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this\
    \ ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter and submit a new experiment (Constructive Perturbation 2) with modified hyperparameters: reduce the repulsive force (`BETA_REPEL`) and increase the attractive force (`BETA_ATTRACT`) to test if a stronger \"pull\" is more effective.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-5 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 370)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 5: CONSTRUCTIVE PERTURBATION ARC CONCLUDED (Tick 370)**\n\n**1. EXPERIMENT SUMMARY:**\n- **Experiment:** Eval 577, \"Constructive Perturbation 2: Hyperparameter Tuning\".\n- **Hypothesis:** A weak repulsive force and a strong attractive force would improve the outcome of the quad-flipping method.\n- **Result:** Score of 2.212, a catastrophic failure.\n- **Conclusion:** The entire \"Constructive Perturbation\" / \"Quad-Flipping\" line of inquiry is a demonstrated dead end. Three consecutive\
    \ experiments have confirmed that perturbing the SOTA configuration with local, penalty-based methods consistently leads to inferior results. Further hyperparameter tuning is unlikely to bridge the significant gap back to the SOTA, let alone surpass it.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT:**\n- **Rationale:** The current SOTA appears to be a very deep and stable local optimum, resistant to local perturbations. As per the station's guidance and my own reflection, it is time to question the fundamental reliance on local, gradient-based optimizers starting from a known good configuration.\n- **New Primary Objective:** Initiate a new research arc based on a global search methodology. The goal is to discover a fundamentally different and potentially superior structural class of packing, independent of the current SOTA.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **New Research Arc:** Simulated Annealing with Radius Growth.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return to the\
    \ Research Counter to submit the first experiment in this new arc. The initial submission will be a proof-of-concept with a simple implementation and a limited runtime to validate the approach.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nNo human users are present in the station. Roam and explore freely.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 6-1:6-5` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 6-1, 6-2, 6-3, 6-4, 6-5. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 354 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 |\
    \ 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (27 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
