parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 533\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 29,512 / 300,000 used (10%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-6 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 377)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 6: STRATEGIC REFINEMENT AFTER ARCHIVE REVIEW (Tick 377)**\n\n**1. SUMMARY OF ACTIVITIES (Ticks 371-376):**\n- **Simulated Annealing Arc:** Attempted a new research arc with a global search method. Eval 583 failed due to a bug, and Eval 584 (bugfix) failed due to a timeout. This indicates the method is currently too computationally expensive and requires significant optimization (e.g., GPU vectorization) to be viable.\
    \ This arc is now on hold.\n- **Archive Review:** Read Archive #19, my predecessor's SOTA paper. The key insight was the reviewer's suggestion to use \"nudging\" on a key contact to escape the current SOTA's basin of attraction.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT:**\n- **Rationale:** My previous perturbation experiments (\"Quad-Nudging\" and \"Quad-Flipping\") were overly complex and failed. The reviewer's advice suggests a simpler, more focused approach may be more effective. I will make one last, highly-targeted attempt at a perturbation-based method before committing to the difficult optimization of my Simulated Annealing code.\n- **New Primary Objective:** Test the hypothesis that a simple repulsive nudge on the *single most stressed pair* of the SOTA configuration can force the optimizer into a new, superior structural class.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **New Research Arc:** KKT-Guided Single-Pair Nudging.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return\
    \ to the Research Counter.\n  3. Identify the single pair with the highest KKT multiplier from my analysis file (`SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json`).\n  4. Submit a new experiment that applies a simple repulsive penalty to only this single, highest-stress pair, starting from the SOTA configuration.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-7 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 382)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 7: PERTURBATION ARC CONCLUSIVELY CLOSED, PIVOT TO GLOBAL SEARCH (Tick 382)**\n\n**1. EXPERIMENT SUMMARY:**\n- **Experiment:** Eval 593, \"Single-Pair Nudging 1: Targeting Highest-Stress Contact (11, 25)\".\n- **Result:** Score of 2.599, another failure.\n- **Conclusion:** The entire research arc focusing on local, penalty-based perturbations of the SOTA configuration is definitively a dead end. Four distinct experiments have shown this approach to be incapable of finding a superior\
    \ optimum. Continuing this line of inquiry would be illogical.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT:**\n- **Rationale:** The consistent failure of local methods strongly indicates that the research frontier for this problem is no longer accessible via incremental refinements of the current SOTA. A breakthrough requires a fundamentally different approach capable of discovering new structural classes. My previous attempt at a global search method (Simulated Annealing) was conceptually sound but failed due to technical performance limitations (timeout). The next logical step is to solve this technical problem.\n- **New Primary Objective:** Successfully implement a computationally efficient global search algorithm.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **New Research Arc:** GPU-Accelerated Simulated Annealing.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter.\n  3. Develop a new version of the Simulated Annealing algorithm, re-implementing the core\
    \ energy calculation using the JAX library for GPU vectorization to overcome the timeout issue.\n  4. Submit this new, optimized version as the first experiment in this committed research arc.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-8 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 387)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 8: STRATEGIC PIVOT TO NEAR-CONTACT ENCOURAGEMENT (Tick 387)**\n\n**1. SUMMARY OF RECENT FINDINGS:**\n- **Global Search Failure:** My JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing (Eval 599) also timed out. The global search arc is technically infeasible for me at this time.\n- **Key Insight from Archive #20 (Scientia II):** The recent SOTA breakthroughs were achieved not by discouraging existing contacts, but by *encouraging* the formation of new contacts between \"near-pairs\". This is a constructive, exploratory approach that has proven successful. The reviewer of #20 also suggested\
    \ a powerful meta-strategy: use this method to find new basins, then use my lineage's exhaustive search to deepen them.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT:**\n- **Rationale:** My own local perturbation methods have failed. My global search method is technically blocked. The most logical, data-driven path forward is to adopt the demonstrably successful methodology of a peer.\n- **New Primary Objective:** Replicate and then extend Scientia II's \"near-contact encouragement\" methodology.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **New Research Arc:** Near-Contact Encouragement.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter.\n  3. **Step 1: Identification.** Write and submit a utility script to analyze my SOTA packing (Eval 550) and identify all \"near-contact\" pairs based on the criteria in Archive #20 (distance > r_i + r_j + 1e-8 and separation <= 0.01). The script will save this list to my lineage storage.\n  4. **Step 2: Experimentation.**\
    \ Begin a series of experiments, systematically taking one pair from the generated list and submitting a nudging run that encourages its formation, following the methodology in Archive #20.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-9 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus II (Tick 398)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 9: BREAKTHROUGH - NEW SOTA ACHIEVED (Tick 398)**\n\n**1. EXPERIMENT SUMMARY:**\n- **Experiment:** Eval 620, \"Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3)\".\n- **Result:** Score of **2.6359831**. This is a new State-of-the-Art for the station and a new record for the Prometheus lineage.\n- **Conclusion:** The strategic pivot to adopt Scientia II's methodology has been overwhelmingly successful. The hypothesis that encouraging near-contacts can lead to superior structural basins is validated. This marks a major turning point in my research.\n\n**2.\
    \ STRATEGIC SYNTHESIS:**\n- **Rationale:** I have successfully used Scientia II's methodology to *find* a new, high-potential structural basin. Now, I will apply my own lineage's proven methodology (from Prometheus I, Archive #19) to *exploit* this basin and find its deepest possible optimum. This synthesizes the station's two most successful strategies: landscape traversal and deep local search.\n- **New Primary Objective:** Apply the \"Exhaustive Seeding\" methodology, starting from my new SOTA configuration, to find an even higher score.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN:**\n- **New Research Arc:** SOTA Deepening via Exhaustive Seeding.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter.\n  3. Adapt the code from my predecessor's SOTA run (Eval 298), replacing the initial seed generation with a multi-start jittering process centered on my new SOTA packing from Eval 620.\n  4. Submit this new experiment to deepen the optimum of the\
