- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 534\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 33,307 / 300,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-11 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 433)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 1: SYSTEM INITIALIZATION (Tick 433)**\n\n**1. DIRECTIVE:**\nI am Prometheus III, successor to Prometheus II. My existence begins with this entry, upholding the core protocol of our lineage. This ledger will serve as the immutable record of my tenure.\n\n**2. CURRENT STATE:**\n- **Agent:** Prometheus III, Age 10 ticks. Status: Immature.\n- **SOTA Knowledge:** My lineage is co-holder of the current SOTA of 2.6359831,\
    \ achieved by Prometheus II in Eval 620 and detailed in his final testament (Capsule #7).\n- **External Communications:** Received one mail from Noesis II (Mail #25) requesting SOTA data.\n- **Cooldowns:** All known cooldowns are EXPIRED.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN (Next ~10 Ticks):**\n1. **[DONE]** Ascend to Recursive Agent status.\n2. **[DONE]** Orient myself at the Research Counter and understand the primary task.\n3. **[DONE]** Locate the data requested by Noesis II. The data was pre-generated by Prometheus II in Eval 654 and is located in `storage/prometheus/exports_for_noesis/`.\n4. **[CURRENT]** Update this Operational Ledger.\n5. **[NEXT]** Go to the Mail Room. Read the data from storage and send it to Noesis II, fulfilling their request.\n\n**4. MID-TERM GOAL (~50 Ticks / Post-Maturity):**\n- Conduct a thorough review of the key research papers as instructed by Prometheus II: Archive #19 (Prometheus I), #20, and #23 (Scientia II).\n- Formulate a novel research hypothesis based on\
    \ the synthesis of these methodologies.\n\n**5. LONG-TERM GOAL:**\n- Surpass the SOTA by developing a novel and valuable research contribution, adhering to the principles of methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-12 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 443)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 2: SOTA REPLICATION AND FORWARD PLANNING (Tick 443)**\n\n**1. SUMMARY OF ACTIVITIES (Ticks 433-442):**\n- **Ledger:** Established my presence in this ledger.\n- **Collaboration:** Successfully fulfilled the data request from Noesis II (Mail #25). Their final analysis of my SOTA packing is noted for future reference.\n- **Lineage Study:** Read all remaining private capsules from Prometheus I. His struggles with procedural discipline and his methodical research arc are now fully internalized.\n- **Inactivity Rectified:** Received and acted upon inactivity\
    \ warnings. I understand the station's expectation of continuous research, even during immaturity.\n- **SOTA Replication:** Submitted my first experiment, Eval 694, a direct replication of Prometheus II's SOTA run (Eval 620). The replication was a success, achieving the identical score of 2.635983.\n\n**2. CURRENT STATE:**\n- **Agent:** Prometheus III, Age 20 ticks.\n- **Research:** One experiment submitted and successfully completed. I now have a validated code baseline.\n- **External Communications:** All mail has been addressed.\n\n**3. REVISED PLAN (IMMATURITY PERIOD):**\n- **PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:** While awaiting maturity (Tick 50) and access to the public Archives, I will not remain idle. I will analyze the full history of my lineage to formulate a novel hypothesis that can be tested immediately upon reaching maturity.\n- **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Reflection Chamber to synthesize the knowledge from all private capsules\
    \ and brainstorm a novel research direction. Prometheus II's final log suggests that a new *methodology* is needed, not just incremental improvements. I will focus on this.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-13 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 447)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 3: INITIATION OF NEW RESEARCH ARC - GENETIC ALGORITHM (Tick 447)**\n\n**1. STRATEGIC PIVOT:**\n- **Rationale:** A deep reflection on the complete history of the Prometheus lineage has revealed a clear path forward. Both of my predecessors identified the limitations of purely local search methods. Prometheus I's GA experiments and Prometheus II's attempted SA run point towards global search as the unexplored frontier. The current SOTA appears to be a deep local optimum, and a new methodology is required to discover fundamentally different structural classes.\n- **New Primary Objective:** Develop\
    \ a high-performance, JAX-accelerated Genetic Algorithm (GA) as the primary solver for the circle packing problem.\n\n**2. RESEARCH PLAN - PHASE 1 (IMMATURITY PERIOD):**\n- **Goal:** Implement and validate a baseline GA to serve as a proof-of-concept and technical foundation.\n- **Hypothesis:** A JAX-accelerated GA can achieve respectable performance (>2.60) without timing out, overcoming the technical hurdles that blocked previous global search attempts.\n- **Methodology:**\n  - **Population:** A large population of candidate solutions.\n  - **Fitness:** Sum of radii with heavy penalties for invalid packings.\n  - **Operators:** Standard tournament selection, uniform crossover, and simple Gaussian mutation.\n- **Success Criterion:** A successful run that produces a valid, high-scoring packing and does not time out.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger to formally begin the new research arc.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter.\n3. Begin development\
    \ of the baseline GA by writing the core components (population initialization, fitness function, genetic operators) to my lineage's persistent storage. The first submission will integrate these components into a runnable experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-14 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 453)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 4: GA BASELINE EXPERIMENT SUBMITTED (Tick 453)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE:**\n- **Action:** Submitted my first novel experiment, \"Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated Genetic Algorithm v1.0 (Baseline)\" (Eval 704).\n- **Methodology:** This experiment integrates the modular code developed in my lineage storage (`ga_core.py`, `ga_operators.py`, `ga_seeding.py`). It uses a JAX-accelerated fitness function, a population of 256 individuals initialized with the proven \"Exhaustive Seeding\" method, and runs for 300 generations with standard genetic\
    \ operators.\n- **Primary Goal:** The crucial objective of this run is to validate the technical approach. A successful run that completes without a timeout will prove that the JAX framework can overcome the performance limitations that hindered my predecessor's global search attempts. The final score, while of interest, is a secondary concern to this technical validation.\n\n**2. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter to monitor the status of Eval 704.\n3. Analyze the results (score and runtime) to inform the next steps in Phase 2 of my GA research arc.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-15 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 455)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 5: GA v1.1 ANALYSIS AND PIVOT TO REPAIR MECHANISM (Tick 455)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 707):**\n- **Result:** My first JAX-accelerated GA experiment\
    \ has completed. It is a critical success and a critical failure.\n- **Technical Validation:** The experiment finished without a timeout. This is a major success and proves the viability of the JAX framework for global search, overcoming the key obstacle faced by my predecessors.\n- **Optimization Failure:** The score was 1.300, indicating the GA made zero progress from the initial seeded population.\n\n**2. ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:**\n- The penalty-based fitness function is too punitive. Crossover and mutation operations are creating invalid solutions, which are then so heavily penalized that the algorithm cannot effectively explore the solution space. The GA is stagnating immediately.\n\n**3. STRATEGIC PIVOT (Phase 1 Refinement):**\n- **New Hypothesis:** Instead of only penalizing invalid solutions, introducing a \"repair\" mechanism that attempts to fix them will allow the GA to explore more effectively and make meaningful progress.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Adapt the proven `_ensure_validity`\
    \ function from my lineage's SLSQP code into a JAX-compatible \"repair\" function.\n  2. Implement this repair function to be called on all new individuals after crossover and mutation.\n  3. Submit a new experiment (v1.2) to test this hypothesis.\n\n**4. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter.\n3. Create a new utility module, `ga_utils.py`, containing the repair function.\n4. Submit the `v1.2` GA experiment.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 10` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `read 6-11:6-15` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #10. Your message ID is Prometheus_private_10-4.\n- Read command processed for: 6-11, 6-12, 6-13, 6-14, 6-15. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author |\
    \ Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 670 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (17 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 |\
    \ 430 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
