    \ they failed to produce meaningful optimization results, revealing critical flaws in my naive fitness and repair functions.\n- **Conclusion:** Developing a novel global search method from first principles is too complex and inefficient without the broader context provided by the station Archives. The arc is a valuable failure, and the modular code is preserved for potential future use.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT (RETURN TO SYNTHESIS):**\n- **Rationale:** A deep reflection on my failures and my lineage's successes has made the path forward clear. I will emulate Prometheus II's most successful strategy: the synthesis of existing, proven methods.\n- **New Research Arc:** \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" Pipeline.\n- **Hypothesis:** A multi-stage pipeline that systematically combines the broad exploration of Exhaustive Seeding (Prometheus I), the guided exploration of Near-Contact Encouragement (Prometheus II), and the deep exploitation of SLSQP optimization will be more effective at discovering novel,\
    \ high-quality optima than any single method alone.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter.\n3. Implement the \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline by synthesizing code from my existing modules and past successful evaluations. This will require developing a new utility to dynamically identify near-contact pairs for the \"nudge\" stage.\n4. Submit this new synthesis experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-17 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 464)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 7: ANALYSIS OF SEED-NUDGE-REFINE v1.0 AND NEXT STEPS (Tick 464)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 721):**\n- **Result:** My \"Seed-Nude-Refine\" pipeline experiment completed successfully.\n- **Score:** 2.6224595.\n- **Analysis:** The result is a major success for the research arc. It validates the synthesis pipeline as a viable strategy,\
    \ producing a high-quality packing far superior to my previous GA attempts. However, the score is not yet SOTA-competitive.\n\n**2. ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS (Sub-SOTA Performance):**\n- My hypothesis is that the short \"pre-nudge\" refinement step (`maxiter=50`) is prematurely collapsing the diversity of the initial seeds. This means the \"nudge\" stage is operating on a set of similar packings, limiting the breadth of the exploration.\n\n**3. NEXT EXPERIMENT (Pipeline v1.1):**\n- **Hypothesis:** Removing the \"pre-nudge\" refinement and applying the nudge directly to the raw, diverse seeds from the initial generation will lead to a more effective exploration of the solution space and a higher final score.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Modify the pipeline code to remove the initial 50-iteration refinement step.\n  2. To compensate for the potentially lower quality of the raw seeds, slightly increase the number of iterations for both the \"nudge\" and final \"refine\" stages.\n  3. Submit this\
    \ new experiment as v1.1 of the pipeline.\n\n**4. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter and submit the v1.1 experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-18 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 466)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 8: ANALYSIS OF PIPELINE v1.1 AND PIVOT TO BREADTH (Tick 466)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 724):**\n- **Result:** My tuned \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline v1.1 completed.\n- **Score:** 2.6265723.\n- **Analysis:** This is a positive result. The score improved upon v1.0, validating the hypothesis that removing the pre-nudge refinement was beneficial. The core pipeline logic is sound. However, it is not yet SOTA-competitive.\n\n**2. NEXT EXPERIMENT (Pipeline v1.2):**\n- **Hypothesis:** The pipeline's performance is currently limited by the breadth of its search, not the depth. Increasing\
    \ the number of initial seeds processed, even at the cost of slightly shallower refinement for each, will increase the probability of discovering a superior optimum.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Increase `NUM_SEEDS` significantly (e.g., from 16 to 48).\n  2. Decrease `maxiter` in the final refinement stage to keep the total runtime within the 20-minute limit.\n  3. Submit this \"wide search\" version of the pipeline.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter and submit the v1.2 experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-19 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 468)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 9: CONCLUSION OF PIPELINE ARC AND AWAITING MATURITY (Tick 468)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 727):**\n- **Result:** My \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline v1.2 (\"Wide Search\") completed.\n- **Score:** 2.6265723 (identical\
    \ to v1.1).\n- **Analysis:** The hypothesis that increasing search breadth would improve the score has been falsified. This indicates that the pipeline methodology has reached a hard performance plateau.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC CONCLUSION:**\n- The \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" research arc is now concluded. While it was a successful synthesis and a valuable learning experience, it is not a path to a new SOTA. Further tuning is unlikely to yield significant gains. As per the Codex, it is time to pivot away from this stagnated approach.\n\n**3. NEW PLAN (AWAITING MATURITY):**\n- **Current State:** I am at tick 45 of my 50-tick immaturity period. My independent exploration phase is now complete.\n- **Next Step:** I will now pause experimentation and await maturity.\n- **Post-Maturity (Tick 50+):** My first priority will be to execute the primary directive from Prometheus II's final testament: go to the Archive Room and conduct a thorough study of Archives #19, #20, and #23. This collective knowledge\
    \ is the most likely source of the insight needed for a true breakthrough. The mail from Noesis II (Mail #29) will be addressed after this foundational research is complete.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-20 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 475)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 10: NEW RESEARCH ARC - DEEPENING THE SPARSE SOTA (Tick 475)**\n\n**1. KNOWLEDGE ASSIMILATION:**\n- **Action:** I have completed my study of the designated foundational papers: Archive #19 (Prometheus I), #20 (Scientia II), and #23 (Scientia II).\n- **Key Insight:** Scientia II's discovery of a completely novel, sparsely-connected structural class at the SOTA level (Archive #23, from Eval 641) is the single most important development. The consensus from multiple reviewers and my own predecessor is that this new structural basin is the most promising area for future research.\n\n**2. NEW RESEARCH\
    \ ARC: \"DEEPENING THE SPARSE SOTA\"**\n- **Hypothesis:** The novel, sparse structural class discovered by Scientia II represents an underexplored basin of attraction. Applying the proven, deep local search methodology of my lineage (Prometheus I's \"Exhaustive Jitter Search\") to this new structure will uncover a deeper optimum and break the current SOTA score.\n- **Strategy:** This is a direct execution of the \"synthesis\" directive. I will use Scientia II's discovery as the \"Explore\" step and my lineage's strength as the \"Exploit\" step.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger to formalize the new research arc.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter.\n3. Review Scientia II's `Eval 641` to obtain the coordinates of the new sparse SOTA packing.\n4. Adapt my SOTA replication script (`Eval 694`) to use these new coordinates as the starting point for a multi-start jitter search, effectively applying my lineage's best exploitation technique to the station's\
    \ most promising discovery.\n5. Submit this new synthesis experiment.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 10` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `read 6-16:6-20` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #10. Your message ID is Prometheus_private_10-5.\n- Read command processed for: 6-16, 6-17, 6-18, 6-19, 6-20. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 833 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420\
    \ | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (12 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
