parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 536\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 41,261 / 300,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-21 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 479)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 11: CONCLUSION OF \"DEEPENING THE SPARSE SOTA\" ARC (Tick 479)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 749):**\n- **Result:** My \"Deepening the Sparse SOTA\" experiment completed successfully after a debugger fix for a random seed error.\n- **Score:** 2.6359774.\n- **Analysis:** The experiment successfully found a deep optimum within the sparse structural basin. However, the score does not surpass the current SOTA. My hypothesis\
    \ that a simple deep search in this new basin would yield a breakthrough is falsified.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC CONCLUSION:**\n- The \"Deepening the Sparse SOTA\" research arc is now concluded. The synthesis of my lineage's exploitation method with Scientia II's discovery has proven robust but not superior. The problem landscape is more challenging than anticipated.\n\n**3. NEW PLAN (RETURN TO INNOVATION):**\n- **Rationale:** Having exhausted the most obvious synthesis strategy, and with my independent exploration having reached its limits, it is time for deep, first-principles thinking. The station is at a SOTA plateau, and incremental improvements or replications are not the path forward.\n- **Next Step:** I will go to the Reflection Chamber to formulate a genuinely novel research hypothesis, informed by my full understanding of the station's history and my own experimental results.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-22 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\
    \n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 483)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 12: INITIATION OF NEW RESEARCH ARC - CONTAINER RELAXATION OPTIMIZATION (CRO) (Tick 483)**\n\n**1. STRATEGIC PIVOT (INNOVATION):**\n- **Rationale:** The station is at a SOTA plateau. My previous synthesis-based experiments, while successful, failed to produce a breakthrough. This indicates that a fundamentally new approach is required, one that challenges the core assumptions of the current optimization paradigm.\n- **New Research Arc:** \"Container Relaxation Optimization\" (CRO).\n\n**2. CORE HYPOTHESIS:**\n- The hypothesis is that the hard boundaries of the unit square create artificial local optima. By allowing the optimizer to first find the most efficient *relative* packing in a slightly larger, \"relaxed\" container, and then scaling the entire superior structure down to fit, we can discover novel and higher-scoring packings that are inaccessible to conventional\
    \ methods. This decouples the search for internal structure from the constraint of absolute size.\n\n**3. EXPERIMENTAL PLAN (CRO v1.0):**\n- **Methodology:** I will adapt my proven multi-start jitter search script (`Eval 749`).\n  1. **Expand:** The `bounds` for the optimizer will be changed from `[0,1]` to `[-0.1, 1.1]`, and the boundary inequality constraint will be removed.\n  2. **Normalize:** A new post-processing function will be added to take the best packing found in the expanded space, calculate its true bounding box, and scale it down to fit perfectly within the unit square.\n\n**4. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter and submit the first CRO experiment.\n3. After the experiment is running, I will begin work on fulfilling the data request from Noesis II (Mail #30).\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-23 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 485)\n\
    \n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 13: ANALYSIS OF CRO v1.0 FAILURE AND BUGFIX PLAN (Tick 485)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 757):**\n- **Result:** My first \"Container Relaxation Optimization\" experiment failed verification due to a minuscule floating-point overlap.\n- **Root Cause Analysis:** In implementing the new `normalize_packing` function, I neglected to apply my lineage's standard `_ensure_validity` function as a final step. This safety function is designed to correct exactly these kinds of precision-related overlaps. This was a procedural error, not a flaw in the CRO hypothesis.\n\n**2. NEXT EXPERIMENT (CRO v1.1 - Bugfix):**\n- **Hypothesis:** The CRO paradigm is sound, and the failure of v1.0 was purely an implementation error. Applying the `_ensure_validity` function after the normalization step will produce a valid packing.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Modify the CRO script to call `_ensure_validity` on the final, normalized packing.\n\
    \  2. Resubmit the experiment as v1.1.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter and submit the bugfixed CRO experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-24 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 487)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 14: CONCLUSION OF CRO ARC AND PIVOT TO HYBRID OPTIMIZATION (Tick 487)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 761):**\n- **Result:** My \"Container Relaxation Optimization\" v1.1 experiment completed.\n- **Score:** 2.154533.\n- **Analysis:** This result decisively falsifies the core CRO hypothesis. The lack of boundary constraints causes the optimizer to find trivial solutions where circles are dispersed with small radii, rather than forming a dense cluster. The research arc is a valuable negative result and is now concluded.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT (RETURN TO HYBRID METHODS):**\n- **Rationale:**\
    \ My high-risk innovation has failed. I will now return to a more pragmatic, iterative approach based on proven concepts. The idea of a global search pre-optimization phase, which both Prometheus II and Quest II have explored (Simulated Annealing), remains a promising direction. It is a more powerful \"seeding\" method than simple jittering.\n- **New Research Arc:** \"Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization\".\n- **Hypothesis:** A single, high-quality candidate solution generated by a computationally-limited Simulated Annealing run will provide a better starting point for a deep SLSQP refinement than either simple jittering or my multi-start pipeline, leading to a SOTA-competitive score.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter to begin addressing the outstanding data requests from Noesis II (Mail #30, #32) as a matter of priority.\n3. After fulfilling community obligations, I will implement and submit the first \"SA-SLSQP\" hybrid\
    \ experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-25 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 491)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 15: COMMUNITY OBLIGATIONS FULFILLED (Tick 491)**\n\n**1. COLLABORATION UPDATE:**\n- **Action:** I have successfully addressed the outstanding data requests from Noesis II (Mail #30, #32, #34).\n- **Method:** I submitted a utility script (Eval 768) that calculated the native-geometry crossing flags for my lineage's SOTA (Eval 620) and saved the data to the shared storage.\n- **Confirmation:** Noesis II has confirmed receipt and integration of the data (Mail #34). My collaborative tasks are now complete.\n\n**2. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter to begin implementation of my new \"Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization\" research arc.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory\
    \ Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive\
    \ Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 10` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `read 6-21:6-25` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #10. Your message ID is Prometheus_private_10-6.\n- Read command processed for: 6-21, 6-22, 6-23, 6-24, 6-25. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words |\
    \ Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 1018 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (7 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (1 unread)\
    \ |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
