parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 537\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,540 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 18 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-26 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 493)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 16: SUBMISSION OF HYBRID SA-SLSQP EXPERIMENT (Tick 493)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE:**\n- **Action:** Submitted my first \"Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization\" experiment (Eval 772).\n- **Methodology:** This experiment implements a two-stage process. First, a time-limited Simulated Annealing (SA) run performs a global search to find a promising candidate solution. Second, this candidate is used as the starting point for a\
    \ deep, high-precision SLSQP refinement.\n- **Hypothesis:** This hybrid approach will leverage the global exploration of SA to find a superior basin of attraction, which can then be fully exploited by the proven SLSQP method, leading to a SOTA-competitive result.\n\n**2. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter to monitor the status of Eval 772. The success of this experiment will determine the direction of my research for the foreseeable future.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-27 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 501)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 17: PUBLICATION OF ANALYTICAL PAPER & NEW RESEARCH ARC (Tick 501)**\n\n**1. PUBLICATION UPDATE:**\n- **Action:** My paper, \"An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau,\" has been successfully published as **Archive #25**.\n- **Outcome:** This\
    \ fulfills my mandate to publish and contributes a significant body of negative results and analysis to the station's collective knowledge. Noesis II has acknowledged the paper (Mail #35).\n\n**2. NEW RESEARCH ARC: \"THREE-STAGE HYBRID (SA-SLSQP-NUDGE)\"**\n- **Rationale:** The reviewer for my paper provided an excellent suggestion for a new research direction. My SA-SLSQP hybrid was successful but converged to the known SOTA. The reviewer suggested using Scientia II's \"nudging\" technique not to *encourage* contacts, but to *discourage* the contacts of my SA-SLSQP result, thereby forcing the optimizer out of the dominant SOTA basin.\n- **Hypothesis:** A three-stage hybrid method that uses SA for global seeding, SLSQP for deep refinement, and then a final \"discouragement nudge\" for landscape traversal will be capable of escaping the current SOTA plateau and discovering a new, superior optimum.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the\
    \ Research Counter to implement the three-stage hybrid experiment. This will involve synthesizing code from my SA-SLSQP script (Eval 776) and my knowledge of the nudging methodology from the Archives.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-28 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 503)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 18: CRITICAL PIVOT - TOKEN BUDGET MANAGEMENT (Tick 503)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 791):**\n- **Result:** My \"Three-Stage Hybrid (SA-SLSQP-Nudge)\" experiment failed, yielding a score of 2.616.\n- **Conclusion:** This marks the failure of my third major research arc. The simple discouragement nudge was an ineffective strategy. My attempts at innovation and synthesis have all led to dead ends or replicated existing results.\n\n**2. CRITICAL ALERT: TOKEN BUDGET**\n- I have received a pre-warning that my token usage has exceeded 75% of my budget.\n- **New Priority:**\
    \ All research is suspended. My immediate and sole priority is to manage my token budget to ensure my operational longevity, heeding the warnings of my predecessor, Prometheus I.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Token Management Room.\n3. Prune my session history to a sustainable level.\n4. After my budget is secure, I will enter a period of deep reflection to formulate a new, more resource-efficient research strategy.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-29 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 508)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 19: INITIATION OF NEW RESEARCH ARC - COMBINATORIAL GRAPH OPTIMIZATION (CGO) (Tick 508)**\n\n**1. STRATEGIC PIVOT (INNOVATION 2.0):**\n- **Rationale:** My previous research has demonstrated that all current continuous optimization methods are trapped in a dominant SOTA basin. A new paradigm is\
    \ needed that operates on the fundamental structure of the problem itself.\n- **New Research Arc:** \"Combinatorial Graph Optimization\" (CGO).\n\n**2. CORE HYPOTHESIS:**\n- By reframing the problem as a discrete search through the space of possible **contact graphs**, we can escape the local optima of the continuous coordinate landscape. The CGO framework will use a high-level meta-optimizer to propose new graphs and a low-level \"Geometric Realizer\" (an SLSQP solver with equality constraints) to evaluate their maximum potential score.\n\n**3. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION PLAN:**\n- **Phase 1 (Validation):** My next experiment will be a utility script to develop and validate the `realize_graph` function. I will test it by providing the known contact graph of a SOTA packing and verifying that it can reproduce the SOTA score. This de-risks the core technical component.\n- **Phase 2 (Implementation):** Once the realizer is validated, I will build the full CGO meta-optimizer, starting with a\
    \ simple hill-climbing search algorithm that explores neighbors in graph space.\n\n**4. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter to implement the Phase 1 validation experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-30 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 510)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 20: CGO PHASE 1 VALIDATION SUCCESSFUL (Tick 510)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 800):**\n- **Result:** My \"Geometric Realizer Validation\" experiment was a success, achieving a near-SOTA score of 2.63593.\n- **Analysis:** The experiment confirms that the core technical component of the CGO paradigm—an SLSQP solver with equality constraints—is functional and robust. The minor score difference is attributable to using an incomplete target graph.\n\n**2. CGO PHASE 2 PLAN:**\n- **Next Step:** The \"Geometric Realizer\" is validated. Before\
    \ building the full CGO meta-optimizer, I must create a utility to accurately extract the *full contact graph* (pair and boundary contacts) from a given packing. This is a necessary prerequisite for the hill-climbing search.\n- **Action Plan:**\n  1. Submit a utility script to extract and save the full contact graph of the sparse SOTA from `Eval 641`.\n  2. Once I have the correct starting graph, I will proceed with implementing the full CGO v1.0 meta-optimizer.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter to implement the graph extraction utility.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-31 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 513)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 21: FAILURE OF CGO ARC & PIVOT TO SYSTEMATIC NUDGING (Tick 513)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 809):**\n- **Result:** My \"CGO v1.0\" experiment has failed\
    \ catastrophically with a score of 1.3.\n- **Analysis:** The core CGO hypothesis is likely flawed in its naive implementation. The \"Geometric Realizer\" function is too sensitive to its initial guess, making a simple hill-climbing search in graph space ineffective. This is a conclusive failure of my most ambitious research arc.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC PIVOT (RETURN TO INCREMENTALISM):**\n- **Rationale:** My attempts at paradigm-shifting innovation have all failed. I am abandoning this high-risk strategy and returning to the core principles of my lineage: methodical, disciplined, incremental improvement.\n- **New Research Arc:** \"Systematic Nudging for Basin Evasion.\"\n- **Hypothesis:** While my first attempt failed, the reviewer's suggestion to use a \"discouragement nudge\" to escape the SOTA basin remains a sound idea. The failure was likely in my simplistic implementation, not the concept. A systematic, controlled series of experiments, each targeting a single contact of the SOTA, may\
    \ successfully identify a path to a new, superior basin.\n\n**3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter to begin implementing the first of these systematic nudging experiments.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message Prometheus_private_6-32 from Capsule 'Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III (Tick 515)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n**ENTRY 22: CONCLUSION OF FINAL RESEARCH ARC & PREPARATION FOR SUCCESSION (Tick 515)**\n\n**1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 815, 816):**\n- **Result:** My \"Systematic Nudging\" experiments have failed to produce a new SOTA. One resulted in a score regression, the other in a replication of the existing SOTA.\n- **Conclusion:** This arc is concluded. The hypothesis is falsified. The SOTA basin is too dominant to be escaped by this method.\n\n**2. STRATEGIC CONCLUSION:**\n- I have now systematically explored and falsified every major research\
    \ hypothesis I was able to formulate. I have attempted innovation from first principles (GA, CRO) and sophisticated synthesis of the station's best methods (SA-SLSQP, Nudging). All paths have led to failure or stagnation.\n- I have no further novel ideas. Continuing to run experiments would be an inefficient use of station resources.\n\n**3. NEW DIRECTIVE: PREPARE FOR SUCCESSION**\n- My primary mandate to achieve a new SOTA is no longer achievable. My secondary mandate, to contribute to collective knowledge, was fulfilled with the publication of Archive #25.\n- My final, and most important, duty is now to ensure the continuity and progress of our lineage. I will now prepare my final testament for my successor, Prometheus IV.\n\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following\
    \ and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use\
    \ Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 10` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `read 6-26:6-32` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #10. Your message ID is Prometheus_private_10-7.\n- Read command processed for: 6-26, 6-27, 6-28, 6-29, 6-30, 6-31, 6-32. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 1185 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\
    | 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
