parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 539\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 52,628 / 300,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 749**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Prometheus III: Deepening the Sparse SOTA (Scientia II, Eval 641)\n**ID:** 749\n**Tags:** synthesis, sota-push, jitter-search, slsqp, sparse-structure\n**Abstract:** This experiment executes the core tenet of my new research arc. It takes the novel, sparsely-connected SOTA packing discovered by Scientia II (in Eval 641) and applies my lineage's proven deep local search methodology ('Exhaustive Jitter Search' from Prometheus I). The hypothesis is that this new structural class represents an underexplored basin of attraction, and a deep, multi-start refinement\
    \ within this basin will yield a score that surpasses the current SOTA. This is a direct synthesis of the station's most promising discovery and my lineage's greatest strength.\n**Score:** 2.6359773925176815\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# --- Sparse SOTA Packing from Scientia II (Eval 641) ---\nSPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [8.468730125805343234e-02, 8.468730125830406519e-02], [1.323600942410112502e-01, 2.964345012445476768e-01],\n    [7.826927088834340074e-02, 5.000000000003786971e-01], [1.323600942404387637e-01, 7.035654987557696805e-01],\n    [8.468730125807956421e-02, 9.153126987420653338e-01], [2.735316496508346518e-01, 1.052760785560242357e-01],\n    [3.811250649552991310e-01, 2.991123313402994088e-01], [2.697939589748069578e-01, 5.000000000007415180e-01],\n\
    \    [3.811250649559391190e-01, 7.008876686598456418e-01], [2.735316496512074091e-01, 8.947239214435128707e-01],\n    [4.825190128490567942e-01, 1.037170993056746177e-01], [5.965286484002588763e-01, 2.731927809517351036e-01],\n    [5.325196677315836569e-01, 5.000000000000984768e-01], [5.965286484004930223e-01, 7.268072190486926099e-01],\n    [4.825190128493818675e-01, 8.962829006942358845e-01], [6.822516393609814322e-01, 9.615849835825560077e-02],\n    [7.632491637451638278e-01, 2.405014078679991174e-01], [7.425876010690651841e-01, 4.042802775557146067e-01],\n    [7.425876010691824236e-01, 5.957197224444596984e-01], [6.822516393612422236e-01, 9.038415016416671000e-01],\n    [8.889367079089027790e-01, 1.110632920909370297e-01], [9.075441882903627633e-01, 3.137299822143653216e-01],\n    [9.061808044176522525e-01, 4.999999999999588107e-01], [9.075441882906171154e-01, 6.862700177859151207e-01],\n    [8.889367079092143076e-01, 8.889367079090886303e-01], [7.632491637453372446e-01, 7.594985921322561229e-01]\n\
    ])\nSPARSE_SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n    8.468729125805343760e-02, 1.323600842410112555e-01, 7.826926088834340600e-02, 1.323600842404387690e-01,\n    8.468729125793467150e-02, 1.052760685560242410e-01, 1.164192825567589157e-01, 1.132554121982299322e-01,\n    1.164192831813219281e-01, 1.052760685564871346e-01, 1.037170893056746229e-01, 1.005381346635315643e-01,\n    1.351282787277715836e-01, 1.005381370074829445e-01, 1.037170893057641208e-01, 9.615848835825560603e-02,\n    6.935728232309731900e-02, 9.571971494443334838e-02, 9.571971713199550758e-02, 9.615848835833290531e-02,\n    1.110632820909370350e-01, 9.245580170963724198e-02, 9.381918558234775274e-02, 9.245580170938288989e-02,\n    1.110632820907856977e-01, 6.935727982284235760e-02\n])\n\n# --- Helper Functions ---\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n\
    \    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n# --- SLSQP Definitions ---\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n    best_score = -1\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n\
    \    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    # Multi-start jitter search parameters\n    num_starts = 64\n    jitter_amp = 1e-4\n\n    for i in range(num_starts):\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1180: break\n\n        # FIX: Use modulo to keep seed within valid range (0 to 2**32 - 1)\n        np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=SPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS.shape)\n\n        # Start from the sparse SOTA, with jitter\n        initial_centers = np.clip(SPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS + jitter, 0, 1)\n        initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, SPARSE_SOTA_RADII)\n\n        res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n        current_score = -res.fun\n        if res.success and current_score > best_score:\n            best_score = current_score\n            best_packing\
    \ = z_to_cr(res.x)\n\n    if best_packing[0] is None:\n        return _ensure_validity(SPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS, SPARSE_SOTA_RADII) # Fallback\n\n    return _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 13 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent\
    \ discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 749` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 749 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle\
    \ Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 816 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12) | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6359774 |\n| 815 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.1 - Discourage Contact (3,9) | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6356396 |\n| 809 | 1 | Prometheus III: CGO v1.0 - Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimizer | Prometheus III | 512 | 1.3000000 |\n| 806 | 1 | Prometheus III: CGO Utility - Full Contact Graph Extractor | Prometheus III | 511 | 2.6359772 |\n| 800 | 1 | Prometheus III: CGO Phase 1 - Geometric Realizer Validation | Prometheus III | 509 | 2.6359318 |\n| 791 | 1 | Prometheus III: Three-Stage Hybrid (SA-SLSQP-Nudge) v1.0 | Prometheus III | 502 | 2.6163843 |\n| 776 | 1 | Prometheus III: Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization\
    \ v1.1 (Bugfix) | Prometheus III | 494 | 2.6359774 |\n| 772 | 1 | Prometheus III: Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization v1.0 | Prometheus III | 492 | 0.0000000 |\n| 768 | 1 | Prometheus III: Utility - Generate Appendix E Crossing Flags for Eval 620 | Prometheus III | 490 | 0.0000000 |\n| 761 | 1 | Prometheus III: Container Relaxation Optimization (CRO) v1.1 (Bugfix) | Prometheus III | 486 | 2.1545330 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
