tick: 542
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My plan is clear: I will implement the next iteration of my \"Constructive Geometry\" arc by replacing the spiral seed generation with a hexagonal lattice seed generation. The rest of the proven SLSQP optimization code will remain the same.\n\n**Implementation Plan:**\n1.  Define a new function `generate_hex_lattice_seed()`.\n2.  This function will generate points on a hexagonal grid.\n3.  It will center this grid at (0.5, 0.5) and take the 26 points closest to the center.\n4.  It will then scale the entire configuration so that the outermost points are just inside the [0,1] square.\n5.  This generated set of centers, along with a small uniform initial radius, will be the input to the optimizer.\n\nI will now submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus IV: Constructive Geometry v1.1 (Hexagonal Lattice Seed)\"\ntags: \"constructive-geometry, geometric-seed, hexagonal-lattice, slsqp\"\nabstract: \"This is the\
    \ second experiment in the Constructive Geometry arc. After the failure of the sparse spiral seed (Eval 861), this experiment tests a dense, geometrically regular seed based on a hexagonal lattice, which is known to be optimal for unconstrained circle packing. The 26 lattice points closest to the center are selected, scaled to fit the unit square, and then used as a single seed for a deep SLSQP refinement. The hypothesis is that this dense, structured initial configuration will lead to a high-quality packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # --- Helper Functions (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n  \
    \        violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  # --- New Geometric Seeding Function ---\n  def generate_hex_lattice_seed():\n      \"\"\"Generates centers from a hexagonal lattice.\"\"\"\n      points = []\n      # Generate a grid larger than needed\n      for i in range(-4, 5):\n          for j in range(-4, 5):\n              x = (i + 0.5 * (j % 2)) * np.sqrt(3)\n              y = j * 1.5\n              points.append((x, y))\n      \n      points = np.array(points)\n      # Center the grid\n      points -= np.mean(points, axis=0)\n      \n      # Find the N points closest to the origin\n      distances = np.linalg.norm(points, axis=1)\n\
    \      sorted_indices = np.argsort(distances)\n      centers = points[sorted_indices[:N]]\n      \n      # Scale to fit into the unit square [0,1] x [0,1]\n      max_abs = np.max(np.abs(centers))\n      centers = centers / (2 * max_abs) + 0.5\n      centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n      # Use a small, uniform initial radius\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n      \n      return centers, initial_radii\n\n  # --- SLSQP Definitions (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Generate the single, deterministic seed\n      initial_centers,\
    \ initial_radii = generate_hex_lattice_seed()\n      initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n      if res.success:\n          final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n          return _ensure_validity(final_centers, final_radii)\n      else:\n          return _ensure_validity(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n```"
