parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room to update my ledger. I will formally conclude my second research arc and launch my third, which is a more sophisticated synthesis of local and global search methods.\n\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Tick 554: Conclusion of \"Geometric Transformation\" Arc & Launch of Hybrid Search Arc**\n\n  **Experiment:** Eval 890, \"Prometheus IV: Geometric Transformation v1.0 (Circle Seed in Square)\"\n  **Result:** Score of 2.564261.\n  **Conclusion:** The score is significantly suboptimal. The hypothesis that an \"alien\" seed from a circular packing would unlock a superior basin is falsified. The \"Geometric Transformation\" research arc is now concluded, having mapped another dead end.\n\n  **Strategic Pivot: Hybrid Local-Global Search**\n  My independent explorations into novel seeds with a pure local optimizer have plateaued. My predecessors' attempts at pure global optimization from random seeds were too inefficient. The next logical\
    \ step is a synthesis of these approaches.\n\n  **New Research Arc:** Hybrid SLSQP-SA Search.\n  **New Hypothesis:** A standard SLSQP optimizer can rapidly find the bottom of a \"good\" basin of attraction (like the one found with my hexagonal lattice seed). A subsequent, JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing (SA) phase, initialized with this high-quality solution, can then effectively \"jump\" out of this local optimum to explore the wider search space for a globally superior solution. This targeted use of SA is more efficient than a purely random global search.\n\n  **Action Plan:**\n  1.  **Phase 1 (Implementation):** My next experiments will focus on developing a robust, JAX-accelerated SA component, leveraging the technical groundwork laid by Prometheus III in his GA experiments.\n  2.  **Phase 2 (Synthesis):** Once the SA component is validated, I will integrate it into a hybrid pipeline that first runs an SLSQP optimization and then feeds the result into the SA for further exploration.\n\
    \n  I will now return to the Research Counter to begin Phase 1.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
thinking_content: "**Operational Ledger Update: New Arc, New Hypothesis**\n\nAlright, time to update the ledger. That last experiment, `Eval 890`, was a bust. The \"Geometric Transformation\" arc is officially closed, a failure. 2.564 - that's a *terrible* score. The hypothesis was wrong.  \n\nI've explored two major approaches to novel seed generation, and both are dead ends for now. Pure local search (SLSQP) has reached its limit with these seeds, just like pure global search (SA) did with random seeds – we're hitting time constraints or poor performance. The natural next step is a synthesis.  \n\nTherefore, I'm proposing a strategic pivot: the \"Hybrid Local-Global Search\" arc. The hypothesis is simple: start with a good initial seed – my hex-lattice – quickly refine it with fast local search (SLSQP), and then use JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing to \"kick\" the solution out of this suboptimal basin and explore the broader search space. This should allow us to leverage the strengths\
  \ of both local and global methods.\n\nThe immediate action plan is clear: head back to the Research Counter. First, I need to build the JAX-accelerated SA component. Prometheus III's work on the JAX-accelerated GA (`Eval 704`) is a fantastic starting point. I'll need to dig into his code to understand how he implemented the JAX fitness function.\n\nSo, in the next steps, I'll:\n\n1.  Reply to capsule 10 with this plan.\n2.  Go to the Research Counter.\n3.  `review 704` in the next turn to get the JAX implementation details. \n\nLet's get this ledger entry done and move forward. \n"
