parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 557\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 97,902 / 300,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 38 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus IV: Hybrid Search v1.0 (JAX SA Validation)' (ID: 894) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7311390042304993\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 0.731139\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 894\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in submission_v2.py. The submission now runs without errors and achieved a score of **0.7311390042304993**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical issues:\n\n1. **Broadcasting Shape Mismatch** (Line 18 in energy_jax):\n   - The code attempted to add `c`\
    \ (shape 26×2) and `r` (shape 26) directly\n   - This caused a ValueError: \"Incompatible shapes for broadcasting: shapes=[(26, 2), (26,)]\"\n   - The boundary violation calculation `c + r - 1.0` failed because JAX couldn't broadcast these incompatible shapes\n\n2. **Missing Helper Function**:\n   - The `z_to_cr()` function was called at line 45 but not defined in the submission\n   - This function converts the internal state vector `z` back to centers and radii arrays\n   - While a version exists in the lineage files (`storage/prometheus/utils/kkt_analyzer.py`), it uses a different data layout (interleaved vs blocked)\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### 1. Added Broadcasting-Compatible Reshape\nIn the `energy_jax` function, I reshaped the radius array to enable proper broadcasting:\n```python\n# Reshape r for broadcasting: (26,) -> (26, 1)\nr_expanded = r[:, None]\n\n# Now this works correctly:\nboundary_violations = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(c + r_expanded - 1.0)) + jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(0.0 - (c - r_expanded)))\n\
    ```\n\nBy expanding `r` from shape (26,) to (26, 1), it can now broadcast correctly with `c` (26, 2) for element-wise operations.\n\n### 2. Added Compatible z_to_cr Function\nCreated a helper function matching the submission's blocked data layout:\n```python\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n    \"\"\"Convert z vector (blocked format) to centers and radii arrays.\"\"\"\n    c = z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2)\n    r = z[N*2:]\n    return c, r\n```\n\nThis matches the submission's z-vector format: [x0, x1, ..., x25, y0, y1, ..., y25, r0, r1, ..., r25]\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: 0.7311390042304993\n- **Fixed Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Execution**: Completed within timeout period using JAX-accelerated simulated annealing\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as\
    \ jnp\nfrom jax import random, jit\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# --- Helper function to convert z to centers and radii ---\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n    \"\"\"Convert z vector (blocked format) to centers and radii arrays.\"\"\"\n    c = z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2)\n    r = z[N*2:]\n    return c, r\n\n# --- JAX-accelerated Energy Function ---\n@jit\ndef energy_jax(z):\n    c = z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2)\n    r = z[N*2:]\n\n    # Reshape r for broadcasting: (26,) -> (26, 1)\n    r_expanded = r[:, None]\n\n    # Boundary penalty (circles must be within [0,1] square)\n    boundary_violations = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(c + r_expanded - 1.0)) + jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(0.0 - (c - r_expanded)))\n\n    # Overlap penalty\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist_sq = jnp.sum(diff**2, axis=-1)\n    iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    dist = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq[iu])\n    rad_sum = r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]\n    overlap_violations = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(rad_sum - dist))\n\n\
    \    # Objective (negative sum of radii) plus a large penalty for violations\n    penalty_weight = 1000.0\n    return -jnp.sum(r) + penalty_weight * (boundary_violations + overlap_violations)\n\n# --- JAX-accelerated Neighbor Function ---\n@jit\ndef neighbor_jax(z, key):\n    # Perturb a random circle's position\n    key, subkey1, subkey2 = random.split(key, 3)\n    move_idx = random.randint(subkey1, shape=(), minval=0, maxval=N)\n    move_vec = random.normal(subkey2, shape=(2,)) * 0.01\n    new_c = z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2).at[move_idx].add(move_vec)\n    return jnp.concatenate([new_c.flatten(), z[N*2:]])\n\n# --- Standard Numpy Validity Checker (for final output) ---\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    c, r = np.array(c), np.array(r)\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n           \
    \     rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n# --- Main Packing Function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    key = random.PRNGKey(int(time.time()))\n\n    # Initial state (random)\n    key, c_key, r_key = random.split(key, 3)\n    initial_c = random.uniform(c_key, shape=(N,2), minval=0.1, maxval=0.9)\n    initial_r = random.uniform(r_key, shape=(N,), minval=0.01, maxval=0.05)\n    current_z = jnp.concatenate([initial_c.flatten(), initial_r])\n    current_energy = energy_jax(current_z)\n\n    best_z = current_z\n    best_energy = current_energy\n\n    # SA Parameters\n    temp = 1.0\n    cooling_rate = 0.99995\n    num_iterations = 100000\n\n    start_time = time.time()\n    for i in range(num_iterations):\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1180: break\n\n        key, subkey = random.split(key)\n\
    \        new_z = neighbor_jax(current_z, subkey)\n        new_energy = energy_jax(new_z)\n\n        delta_e = new_energy - current_energy\n\n        key, subkey = random.split(key)\n        acceptance_prob = jnp.exp(-delta_e / temp)\n\n        if (delta_e < 0) or (random.uniform(subkey) < acceptance_prob):\n            current_z, current_energy = new_z, new_energy\n            if current_energy < best_energy:\n                best_z, best_energy = current_z, current_energy\n\n        temp *= cooling_rate\n\n    final_c, final_r = z_to_cr(best_z)\n    return _ensure_validity(final_c, final_r)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write storage/prometheus/hybrid_solver_v1.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: prometheus/hybrid_solver_v1.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 894 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Hybrid Search v1.0 (JAX SA Validation) | Prometheus IV | 555 | 0.7311390 |\n| 890 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Geometric Transformation v1.0 (Circle Seed in Square) | Prometheus IV | 552 | 2.5642608 |\n| 883 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Geometric Transformation Utility v1.1 (Bugfix) | Prometheus IV | 549 | 2.2793154 |\n| 881 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Geometric Transformation Utility v1.0 (Circle Pack Solver) | Prometheus IV | 548 | 0.0000000 |\n| 874 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Synthesis v1.0 (Hex-Lattice Seed + Jitter Search) | Prometheus\
    \ IV | 545 | 2.6134507 |\n| 870 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Constructive Geometry v1.1 (Hexagonal Lattice Seed) | Prometheus IV | 542 | 2.6021479 |\n| 861 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Constructive Geometry v1.0 (Archimedean Spiral Seed) | Prometheus IV | 539 | 0.8543484 |\n| 816 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12) | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6359774 |\n| 815 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.1 - Discourage Contact (3,9) | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6356396 |\n| 809 | 1 | Prometheus III: CGO v1.0 - Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimizer | Prometheus III | 512 | 1.3000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
