tick: 563
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to launch my new \"Optimizer Exploration\" arc. I will take my most successful script to date (`Eval 874`, which combined a hexagonal lattice seed with a multi-start jitter search) and make a single, critical change: switching the optimization method from `SLSQP` to `L-BFGS-B`.\n\n**Implementation Note:**\nThe `L-BFGS-B` method in `scipy.optimize.minimize` does not support `constraints` in the same way `SLSQP` does. It only supports `bounds`. This means I cannot pass my non-overlap inequality constraints directly to the optimizer. To handle this, I will move the non-overlap and boundary violation checks into the objective function itself, as a large penalty term. This is a common technique for adapting constraint-based problems to optimizers that don't natively support them. It is essentially the same \"energy function\" approach I used in my JAX SA experiments, but implemented in standard NumPy.\n\nI will now submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus IV: Optimizer Exploration v1.0 (L-BFGS-B)\"\ntags: \"optimizer-exploration, l-bfgs-b, hexagonal-lattice, jitter-search\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment in the 'Optimizer Exploration' arc, questioning my lineage's fundamental reliance on SLSQP. This script uses my best-performing setup (multi-start jitter search on a hexagonal lattice seed) but replaces the SLSQP optimizer with L-BFGS-B. Because L-BFGS-B does not support inequality constraints, the non-overlap and boundary conditions have been moved into the objective function as a large penalty term. The hypothesis is that this different optimization algorithm will traverse the search landscape differently and may discover a new, superior optimum.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # --- Helper Functions ---\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(),\
    \ r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  # --- Seeding Function ---\n  def generate_hex_lattice_seed():\n      points = []\n      for i in range(-4, 5):\n          for j in range(-4, 5):\n              x = (i + 0.5 * (j % 2)) * np.sqrt(3); y = j * 1.5\n              points.append((x, y))\n      points = np.array(points)\n      points -= np.mean(points, axis=0)\n      distances = np.linalg.norm(points, axis=1)\n      sorted_indices\
    \ = np.argsort(distances)\n      centers = points[sorted_indices[:N]]\n      max_abs = np.max(np.abs(centers))\n      centers = centers / (2 * max_abs) + 0.5\n      centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n      return centers, initial_radii\n\n  # --- Objective function for L-BFGS-B (with penalties) ---\n  def objective_with_penalties(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      \n      # Boundary penalty\n      boundary_violations = np.sum(np.maximum(0, c + r - 1.0)) + np.sum(np.maximum(0, 0.0 - (c - r)))\n      \n      # Overlap penalty\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      rad_sum = r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]\n      overlap_violations = np.sum(np.maximum(0, rad_sum - dist))\n      \n      penalty_weight = 1000.0\n      return -np.sum(r) + penalty_weight * (boundary_violations + overlap_violations)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n\
    \      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      \n      base_centers, base_radii = generate_hex_lattice_seed()\n\n      num_starts = 64\n      jitter_amp = 1e-3\n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1180: break\n\n          np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n          jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n          initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 0, 1)\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n\n          res = minimize(objective_with_penalties, initial_z, method='L-BFGS-B', bounds=bounds, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          # Score is the negative of the objective, but we must re-calculate without penalties\n          # to get the true score.\n          final_c, final_r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n          # First, ensure the packing is valid\n          valid_c,\
    \ valid_r = _ensure_validity(final_c, final_r)\n          current_score = np.sum(valid_r)\n          \n          if res.success and current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_packing = (valid_c, valid_r)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n\n      return best_packing\n```"
