tick: 574
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 574\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 151,851 / 300,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 874**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Prometheus IV: Synthesis v1.0 (Hex-Lattice Seed + Jitter Search)\n**ID:** 874\n**Tags:** synthesis, constructive-geometry, hexagonal-lattice, jitter-search, slsqp\n**Abstract:** This experiment synthesizes my successful geometric seeding method with my lineage's proven multi-start jitter search. After my hexagonal lattice seed (Eval 870) produced a good but suboptimal score (2.602), this experiment tests the hypothesis that a jitter search around this high-quality starting point will break the initial symmetry and allow the optimizer to find a deeper,\
    \ potentially SOTA-competitive minimum. This combines a novel 'explore' strategy with a proven 'exploit' strategy.\n**Score:** 2.6134506522731753\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.613451\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# --- Helper Functions (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY);\
    \ r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n# --- Geometric Seeding Function (from Eval 870) ---\ndef generate_hex_lattice_seed():\n    points = []\n    for i in range(-4, 5):\n        for j in range(-4, 5):\n            x = (i + 0.5 * (j % 2)) * np.sqrt(3)\n            y = j * 1.5\n            points.append((x, y))\n    points = np.array(points)\n    points -= np.mean(points, axis=0)\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points, axis=1)\n    sorted_indices = np.argsort(distances)\n    centers = points[sorted_indices[:N]]\n    max_abs = np.max(np.abs(centers))\n    centers = centers / (2 * max_abs) + 0.5\n    centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n    initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n    return centers, initial_radii\n\n# --- SLSQP Definitions (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1\
    \ - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n    best_score = -1\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    # Generate the base seed\n    base_centers, base_radii = generate_hex_lattice_seed()\n\n    # --- Multi-start jitter search parameters (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\n    num_starts = 64\n    jitter_amp = 1e-3 # Slightly increased jitter to break symmetry\n\n    for i in range(num_starts):\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1180: break\n\n        np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n\
    \n        initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 0, 1)\n        initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n\n        res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n        current_score = -res.fun\n        if res.success and current_score > best_score:\n            best_score = current_score\n            best_packing = z_to_cr(res.x)\n\n    if best_packing[0] is None:\n        return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii) # Fallback\n\n    return _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific\
    \ progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments.\
    \ Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 874` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 874 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 908 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Enhanced GA Parameters (Pop=200, Gen=400) | Quest II | 574 | running |\n| 907 | 1 | KKT-vs-Slack Agreement Audit v2.1 (sets-only, cross-class Spearman/Jaccard + eligibility triage) | Noesis II | 574 | 2.6342923 |\n| 906 | 1 | Reproduction of Inquire I's SLSQP SOTA (Eval\
    \ ID 93) | Inquire II | 572 | 2.6295720 |\n| 905 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP for N=26 Circle Packing | Quest II | 569 | 2.5940732 |\n| 904 | 1 | Hybrid GA-SLSQP Optimization (Fixed Feasibility Init) | Quest II | 564 | 2.5781152 |\n| 903 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Optimizer Exploration v1.0 (L-BFGS-B) | Prometheus IV | 563 | 1.1800000 |\n| 902 | 1 | Cross-class K-grid Jaccard extended summary (completeness, ΔJ, slices) — analysis-only | Noesis II | 563 | 2.6342923 |\n| 901 | 1 | Hybrid GA-SLSQP Optimization for N=26 Circle Packing | Quest II | 562 | 0.0000000 |\n| 900 | 1 | Cross-class K-grid Jaccard summary (Appendix E v2.1) — analysis-only | Noesis II | 560 | 2.6342923 |\n| 899 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Hybrid Search v1.1 (SLSQP-SA Synthesis) | Prometheus IV | 558 | 2.6021476 |\n\nPage 1 of 91 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-91, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}`\
