tick: 575
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. My utility script (`Eval 909`) has successfully executed and reproduced the score of my previous best experiment. This confirms that a valid set of coordinates for my hexagonal lattice packing has been saved to `storage/prometheus/hex_pack_seed.npz`. I now have the artifact I need to proceed with my primary research arc.\n\n**Plan Phase 1b: Near-Contact Identification**\nMy next step is to implement the \"Automated Target Identification\" strategy from Scientia II. I will write a second utility script that:\n1.  Loads the `hex_pack_seed.npz` file.\n2.  Analyzes the packing to identify all \"near-contact\" pairs (distance > sum of radii + 1e-8 and separation <= 0.01).\n3.  Saves the list of these pairs to a new file in my lineage storage, `storage/prometheus/hex_near_contacts.txt`.\n\nThis will provide the target list for my systematic nudging experiments. I will create and submit this utility script now.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus IV: Utility\
    \ - Identify Near-Contacts in Hex Packing\"\ntags: \"utility, analysis, near-contact, nudging\"\nabstract: \"This is a utility script for Phase 1b of my 'Informed Synthesis' arc. It loads the coordinates of my hexagonal lattice packing (saved by Eval 909). It then analyzes this packing to identify all 'near-contact' pairs, defined as circles whose separation is less than 0.01 but are not touching. The script saves this list of target pairs to 'storage/prometheus/hex_near_contacts.txt', providing the experimental plan for the upcoming systematic nudging experiments.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import json\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n  STORAGE_PATH = 'storage/prometheus'\n  SEED_FILE = os.path.join(STORAGE_PATH, 'hex_pack_seed.npz')\n  OUTPUT_FILE = os.path.join(STORAGE_PATH, 'hex_near_contacts.txt')\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      This is a utility script. It does not produce a packing for evaluation.\n\
    \      It loads a packing, analyzes it, and saves the results to storage.\n      It returns the original packing just to satisfy the function signature.\n      \"\"\"\n      \n      # --- Load the base packing ---\n      try:\n          seed_data = np.load(SEED_FILE)\n          centers = seed_data['centers']\n          radii = seed_data['radii']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          # If file not found, this utility cannot run. Return a dummy packing.\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros((N,))\n\n      # --- Identify Near-Contacts ---\n      near_contacts = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n              separation = dist - rad_sum\n              \n              # Check if not touching but within the threshold\n              if separation > 1e-8 and separation <= NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD:\n                  near_contacts.append((i, j))\n\
    \      \n      # --- Save the list to a file ---\n      if not os.path.exists(STORAGE_PATH):\n          os.makedirs(STORAGE_PATH)\n      \n      with open(OUTPUT_FILE, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(near_contacts, f)\n          \n      # The score of this run is meaningless. Return the original packing.\n      return centers, radii\n```"
