tick: 579
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully read the target file. The closest non-contact pair in my hexagonal packing is `(8, 10)`.\n\nI will now submit the definitive experiment for this arc. The script will load my hexagonal packing, apply the \"nudging\" penalty to encourage contact between circles 8 and 10, and then run a multi-start SLSQP optimization. This is the culmination of my synthesis strategy.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus IV: Synthesis v1.1 (Nudging Closest Hex Pair)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, nudging, hexagonal-lattice, slsqp\"\nabstract: \"This is the core experiment of my 'Informed Synthesis' arc. It tests a novel combination of strategies: applying the SOTA 'nudging' technique to my unique hexagonal lattice packing. After discovering this packing has no 'near-contacts', this experiment targets the single closest pair (8, 10) for contact encouragement. The hypothesis is that this targeted perturbation, starting from a structurally distinct, high-quality configuration,\
    \ will force the optimizer into a new basin of attraction and yield a SOTA-competitive score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n  import os\n  import json\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n  STORAGE_PATH = 'storage/prometheus'\n  SEED_FILE = os.path.join(STORAGE_PATH, 'hex_pack_seed.npz')\n  TARGET_FILE = os.path.join(STORAGE_PATH, 'hex_closest_pair.txt')\n\n  # --- Helper Functions ---\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1;\
    \ scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  # --- Nudging Objective Function (Adapted from Archive #20) ---\n  def create_penalized_objective(pairs_to_encourage):\n      # Nudging parameters from Scientia II\n      ALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2\n      EPS_CLOSE = 0.005\n      \n      def objective_penalized(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          base_objective = -np.sum(r)\n          \n          encouragement_penalty = 0\n          for i, j in pairs_to_encourage:\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n              rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n              penalty = np.maximum(0, dist - (rad_sum + EPS_CLOSE))**2\n              encouragement_penalty += penalty\n              \n          return base_objective + ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * encouragement_penalty\n      return objective_penalized\n\n  # --- Standard Constraint Functions ---\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return\
    \ np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]; dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n\n      # --- Load base packing and target pair ---\n      try:\n          seed_data = np.load(SEED_FILE)\n          base_centers = seed_data['centers']\n          base_radii = seed_data['radii']\n          with open(TARGET_FILE, 'r') as f:\n              target_pairs = json.load(f)\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          # Fallback if files don't exist\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros((N,))\n          \n      # Create the specific objective function for this run\n      objective_func = create_penalized_objective(target_pairs)\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2\
    \ + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      num_starts = 64\n      jitter_amp = 1e-3\n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1180: break\n\n          np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n          jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n          initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 0, 1)\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n\n          res = minimize(objective_func, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if res.success:\n              final_c, final_r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n              valid_c, valid_r = _ensure_validity(final_c, final_r)\n              current_score = np.sum(valid_r)\n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  best_score = current_score\n   \
    \               best_packing = (valid_c, valid_r)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n\n      return best_packing\n```"
