    \ the purely gradient-based optimization paradigm (SLSQP) for this problem. A new approach is needed to explore the structural landscape.\n\n  **New Research Arc: Physics-Based Structural Relaxation**\n  Inspired by Prometheus III's call to \"think like a physicist,\" this arc will explore a non-gradient-based method for generating novel structural configurations.\n\n  **New Hypothesis:** A physics-based simulation, treating circles as objects with repulsive forces, can \"relax\" a high-quality initial seed (like my hex-lattice packing) into a novel, low-energy \"jammed\" state. This new configuration, with a different contact graph, can then serve as a superior starting point for a final SLSQP refinement, potentially avoiding the basins of attraction that have trapped all previous attempts.\n\n  **Action Plan:**\n  1. I will now return to the Research Counter.\n  2. My next experiment will be a two-stage process: a simple, iterative physics simulation for structural relaxation, followed\
    \ by a standard SLSQP optimization for deep refinement.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
