- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 589\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus IV\n- Agent Description: Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 182,329 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 927**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Experiment 4: SOTA-Seeded GA + SLSQP Hybrid\n**ID:** 927\n**Tags:** episteme, genetic algorithm, hybrid method, sota seeding, elitism\n**Abstract:** After the previous GA-hybrid scored poorly, this experiment improves the method by seeding the initial GA population with the current SOTA packing.\nBy placing the best-known solution directly into the gene pool, the GA can explore mutations and crossovers in the immediate vicinity of the SOTA, a much more promising search space.\nThe rest of the population remains random to encourage diversity. The goal is\
    \ for the GA to evolve a solution that surpasses the SOTA from which it originated.\n**Score:** 2.6359830822816064\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\nN = 26\n\n# --- Genetic Algorithm Components ---\nPOPULATION_SIZE = 20\nGENERATIONS = 50\nMUTATION_RATE = 0.1\nMUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.05\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r, repair_iters=10):\n    for _ in range(repair_iters):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations += 1\n                    scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n                    r[i] *= scale\n                    r[j] *= scale\n        if violations == 0:\n            break\n    r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1)\n    c = np.clip(c,\
    \ r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-6)\n\ndef create_individual():\n    centers = np.random.rand(N, 2)\n    radii = np.random.uniform(0.05, 0.1, size=N)\n    return _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n\ndef fitness(individual):\n    return np.sum(individual[1])\n\ndef crossover(parent1, parent2):\n    c1, r1 = parent1; c2, r2 = parent2\n    mask = np.random.rand(N) < 0.5\n    child_r = np.where(mask, r1, r2)\n    child_c = np.where(mask[:, np.newaxis], c1, c2)\n    return child_c, child_r\n\ndef mutate(individual):\n    centers, radii = individual\n    if np.random.rand() < MUTATION_RATE:\n        idx = np.random.randint(N)\n        centers[idx] += np.random.uniform(-MUTATION_STRENGTH, MUTATION_STRENGTH, 2)\n        radii[idx] *= np.random.uniform(1 - MUTATION_STRENGTH, 1 + MUTATION_STRENGTH)\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    np.random.seed(42)\n    # --- Stage 1: Genetic Algorithm with SOTA Seeding ---\n    population = [create_individual()\
    \ for _ in range(POPULATION_SIZE - 1)]\n    try:\n        sota_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_centers.txt')\n        sota_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_radii.txt')\n        population.append((sota_centers, sota_radii))\n    except Exception:\n        population.append(create_individual()) # Add one more random if SOTA fails to load\n    \n    for gen in range(GENERATIONS):\n        population.sort(key=fitness, reverse=True)\n        # Elitism: Keep the best individual\n        next_gen = [population[0]]\n        while len(next_gen) < POPULATION_SIZE:\n            p1_idx, p2_idx = np.random.choice(POPULATION_SIZE // 2, 2, replace=False)\n            child_c, child_r = crossover(population[p1_idx], population[p2_idx])\n            child_c, child_r = mutate((child_c, child_r))\n            child_c, child_r = _ensure_validity(child_c, child_r)\n            next_gen.append((child_c, child_r))\n        population = next_gen\n\n    best_ga_packing = max(population,\
    \ key=fitness)\n    ga_centers, ga_radii = best_ga_packing\n    \n    # --- Stage 2: SLSQP Refinement ---\n    def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n    def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n    def ineq_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n    def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]; dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n    \n    initial_z = cr_to_z(ga_centers, ga_radii)\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    \n    if\
    \ res.success:\n        c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n        return _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n    else:\n        return ga_centers, ga_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Noesis II**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 589.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 927` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 927 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task\
    \ ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 934 | 1 | Experiment 6: Greedy + SLSQP Hybrid (v1) | Episteme III | 588 | 2.6098028 |\n| 933 | 1 | Utility: Replicate & Store Champion Packing for KKT (from Eval ID 922) | Quest II | 588 | running |\n| 932 | 1 | Experiment 5: Greedy Constructive Heuristic (v1) | Episteme III | 587 | 1.4581765 |\n| 931 | 1 | Final Verification of Trust-Constr Baseline with KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 587 | 2.5520180 |\n| 930 | 1 | Debug Trust-Constr Method String for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 585 | 2.5520180 |\n| 929 | 1 | Prometheus IV: Physics-Based Search v1.1 (Radius Growth + SLSQP) | Prometheus IV | 585 | 2.5991607 |\n| 928 | 1 | Verified Trust-Constr Baseline (No Debugger Required) for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 584 | 2.5520180 |\n| 927 | 1 | Experiment 4: SOTA-Seeded GA + SLSQP Hybrid | Episteme III | 583 | 2.6359831 |\n| 926 | 1 | Experiment 3.1: GA + SLSQP Hybrid (Validity\
    \ Fix) | Episteme III | 582 | 2.5661130 |\n| 925 | 1 | Verified Trust-Constr Baseline for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 582 | 2.5520180 |\n\nPage 1 of 94 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-94, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
