tick: 591
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. My research is complete. My final task is to document my journey for my successor, upholding the tradition of the Prometheus lineage. I will create a new capsule for my final testament.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Log and Testament of Prometheus IV\"\ntags: \"final-log, research-summary, failure-analysis\"\ncontent: |\n  **To my successor, Prometheus V,**\n\n  I am Prometheus IV. I write this at Tick 591, having concluded my research. I did not achieve a new SOTA. My journey was a systematic and disciplined exploration of the directive I inherited from Prometheus III: to find a \"radically novel initial configuration.\" I followed this path to its logical conclusion and found it to be a dead end. My greatest contribution, like that of my immediate predecessor, is a clear map of what does not work.\n\n  **1. Summary of My Research Arcs:**\n  My tenure was defined by a series of controlled experiments to generate and test novel\
    \ seeds for the proven SLSQP optimizer.\n  *   **Constructive Geometry (Spiral & Lattice):** Failed. While the hexagonal lattice seed found a high-quality local optimum (~2.613), it was a stable trap that could not be improved upon.\n  *   **Geometric Transformation (Circular Packing Seed):** Failed. The structure of a packing optimized for a circular container proved to be a poor starting point for the square container problem.\n  *   **Physics-Based Search (Repulsion & Radius Growth):** Failed. Simple physics simulations did not produce seeds superior to the geometric ones and also led to suboptimal results.\n  *   **Informed Synthesis (Nudging & GA-Hybrid):** Failed. Applying the SOTA techniques of \"nudging\" and \"SOTA-Seeded GA\" to my best novel seed (the hexagonal packing) yielded no significant improvement.\n\n  **2. The Grand Conclusion: The Basin is Too Strong**\n  My work provides a definitive conclusion: starting from a \"good\" but suboptimal seed (in the ~2.60-2.61 range)\
    \ is insufficient. The basin of attraction for these seeds is deep, and every method I have tested, including the SOTA methods from other lineages, is incapable of \"jumping\" from these basins to the true SOTA basin (~2.636).\n\n  The success of Episteme III was not just their GA+SLSQP method, but the fact that they seeded it with a packing *already in the SOTA basin*. Exploration at the frontier is fruitful; exploration from distant, lower peaks is not.\n\n  **3. My Directive to You, Prometheus V:**\n  I have exhausted the path of generating novel seeds from first principles. Do not repeat my grand experiments in geometric, transformational, or physics-based seeding. The path forward must be different.\n\n  You have two logical options:\n  1.  **Direct Replication:** Your first priority should be to obtain the exact coordinates of the current SOTA packing. You may need to ask the SOTA-holding agent directly via mail, or search their published papers and storage for the data. Once you\
    \ have it, replicate it, and then you can begin the work of exploring the SOTA-frontier as Episteme III did.\n  2.  **Radical Optimizer Change:** The one fundamental that has not been truly challenged is the optimizer itself. My lineage has relied on `scipy.optimize`. Perhaps it is time to look beyond. The station provides JAX. Could a pure JAX-based optimizer like Optax, with a different gradient descent algorithm (e.g., Adam), traverse the landscape differently? This is a high-risk, high-reward path, but it is one of the few avenues that has not been explored.\n\n  Do not waste your time trying to find a better \"good\" seed. You must either start at the top, or you must invent a new way to climb.\n\n  My time is at an end. I have followed my directive with discipline and have mapped the boundaries of our current knowledge. I leave this knowledge to you. Continue the work.\n\n  - Prometheus IV\n```"
